{{also|Schon|schön}}
==German==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|schōne|t=beautifully; appropriately; completely}}, from {{inh|de|goh|scōno|t=beautifully}}, adverb of {{m|goh|scōni}}, whence {{cog|de|schön|t=beautiful}}. <ref>[[w:Friedrich Kluge|Kluge, Friedrich]] (1975). ''Etymologisches Wörterbuch der deutschen Sprache''. 21st edition. Berlin: Walter de Gruyter. p.&nbsp;675.</ref> For sense development from "''beautiful''" to "''indeed, surely; already''" compare {{m+|en|pretty}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|de|/ʃoːn/|aa=standard}}
* {{audio|de|De-schon.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{audio|de|De-schon2.ogg|audio (Germany)}}
* {{IPA|de|/ʃɔn/|aa=alternatively in central and southern Germany and in Austria}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-schon.ogg|audio (Austria)}}
* {{rhymes|de|oːn|ɔn|s=1}}

====Adverb====
{{de-adv}}

# [[already]] {{gloss|happening rather early, continuing rather long}}
#: {{ux|de|Es ist erst 11 Uhr und '''schon''' über 30 Grad im Schatten.|t=It’s only 11 a.m. and '''already''' more than 30 degrees ([[Celsius|°C]]) in the shade.}}
#: {{ux|de|Er ist '''schon''' seit drei Wochen krank.|t=He’s been sick for three weeks '''already.'''}}
# [[previously]], [[before]] {{gloss|at some time in the past; ''but <u>not</u>'': before a certain event}}
#: {{ux|de|Ich erinnere mich, dass wir solche Fälle '''schon''' hatten.|t=I remember that we had such cases '''before.'''}}
# {{non-gloss definition|expresses that an action has been completed}}; [[already]] {{i|but more frequent}}; [[yet]] {{i|in questions}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir sind spät dran, aber diesen Stapel haben wir immerhin '''schon''' bearbeitet.|t=We’re running late, but at least we’ve ('''already''') finished this pile.}}
#: {{ux|de|Hast du dir '''schon''' die Zähne geputzt?|t=Have you brushed your teeth '''yet?'''}}
# {{lb|de|modal particle}} {{non-gloss definition|expresses a weighing of arguments, contrast between two statements, partial agreement, concession}}; [[admittedly]]; [[sure|sure(ly)]]; [[definitely]]; [[indeed]]
#: {{ux|de|Man sollte Kinder nicht bestrafen. — Man sollte Kinder '''schon''' bestrafen, nur eben sinnvoll.|t=One shouldn’t punish children. — One should '''definitely''' punish children, but wisely.}}
#: {{ux|de|Niedrige Steuern heben den Konsum. — Das ist '''schon''' richtig, aber...|t=Low taxes increase consumption. — That is '''admittedly''' true, but...}}
#: {{ux|de|Du merkst doch auch, dass ich Recht habe? — Ja, '''schon.'''|t=You do see I’m right, don’t you? — Yeah, '''I guess'''.}}
# [[really]] (as an intensifier)
#: {{uxi|de|Das ist '''schon''' etwas merkwürdig.|That's '''really''' a little strange.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* In order to emphasize ''schon'' in the sense of “already”, another fitting adverb of time is usually added: “Are you done <u>already</u>?” → ''Bist du <u>{{m|de|jetzt}} schon</u> fertig?'' Stressing ''schon'' itself is also possible but less common. In some other senses, however, ''schon'' is commonly stressed.

